    add_body_p(doc, "The coursework focuses on the architectural design, implementation, and comprehensive quality assurance of a client-server web system for equipment rental featuring a per-unit availability calendar. The system enforces strict domain invariants: preventing double booking of physical inventory units while accounting for mandatory post-rental maintenance buffers (maintenance_buffer_hours), executing exact monetary calculations in integer minor units (kopiykas) for base rates, security deposits, and late return penalties, and managing an automated waitlist (Waitlist) when requested time slots are occupied.")
    add_body_p(doc, "The backend is engineered using C# and ASP.NET Core 10.0 Web API following Clean Architecture principles, backed by SQLite 3 in Write-Ahead Logging (WAL) mode with parameterized SQL queries and immediate write transactions (BEGIN IMMEDIATE) to eliminate race conditions under concurrent requests. The frontend is built as a responsive React 19 Single-Page Application (SPA) compliant with WCAG 2.2 Level AA accessibility guidelines across 360px, 768px, and 1280px viewports. Experimental verification demonstrates 100% pass rate across unit, integration, and Playwright end-to-end tests, a 3.07x query speedup at 10,000 booking records via composite B-Tree indexing, and stable sub-10 ms p99 latency under 25 concurrent virtual users.")
